From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:16:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fb: fbCopyWindow copies in the window pixmap's coordinates
 (Composite)

A redirected window's pixmap covers only the window, placed at screen_x,
screen_y; fbCopyWindow passed the window's border clip in screen
coordinates to fbCopyRegion on that pixmap, so moving a child window of a
redirected window copied rows of the wrong place, past the pixmap's end
for a window low on the screen (JWM's tray after the screen grew: a
segfault in fbBlt).  The region is translated by -screen_x, -screen_y,
as X.Org's fbCopyWindow does under COMPOSITE.
---
 fb/fbwindow.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fb/fbwindow.c b/fb/fbwindow.c
index d687481..44c9762 100644
--- a/fb/fbwindow.c
+++ b/fb/fbwindow.c
@@ -127,7 +127,12 @@ fbCopyWindow(WindowPtr pWin, DDXPointRec ptOldOrg, RegionPtr prgnSrc)
 
     REGION_INTERSECT(&rgnDst, &pWin->borderClip,
                      prgnSrc);
-
+#ifdef COMPOSITE
+    /* a redirected window's pixmap covers only the window, at screen_x,
+       screen_y: the copy is in the pixmap's coordinates (as in X.Org) */
+    if (pPixmap->screen_x || pPixmap->screen_y)
+        REGION_TRANSLATE(&rgnDst, -pPixmap->screen_x, -pPixmap->screen_y);
+#endif
 
     fbCopyRegion(pDrawable, pDrawable,
                  0, &rgnDst, dx, dy, fbCopyWindowProc, 0, 0);
